  "stem": "If \\(x + \\frac{6}{x} = 5\\) and \\(x > 2\\), what is the value of \\(x\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "3"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Multiply both sides by \\(x\\): \\(x^{2} + 6 = 5x\\), so \\(x^{2} - 5x + 6 = 0\\).",
    "Factor: \\((x - 2)(x - 3) = 0\\), so \\(x = 2\\) or \\(x = 3\\). Since \\(x > 2\\), \\(x = 3\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nsols = solve(Eq(x + 6/x, 5), x)\nassert set(sols) == {2, 3}\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == 3",
